{
 "case": "CAP-09",
 "says": "A person founds a Team on their own (team.found, self-founded, threshold 0): the owner commits the sealed proposal, the policy, the founder's membership, a grant that lets the founder contribute in the Team, the Team's state and profile and its founding authority epoch. The Team then registers a decision source of its own (source.home.register). The person selects one span of a repository session transcript (source.observe) whose selection permits results in both that repository and that Team, and captures a memory entry from it for the Team decision source, at the head its registration committed, stating the widening: the repository scope it came from, the applicability it proposes (a shared network volume), and the founder's grant as the authority to widen (source.capture.record). The owner stores that capture as a draft with its extraction run, and the person stores a candidate from it for the same Team destination (memory.candidate.store). Four attempts to widen otherwise must fail and leave nothing stored: the same capture sent to the Team without the widening is refused with widening_unstated; one that states the widening but names no authority is refused at admission (missing_field at /widens/authority_evidence_digest); one whose input permits only the repository is refused with input_not_permitted at the input's permits, returning no output, so no private evidence reaches the Team; and one that restates the same material as widened from a second Team's scope (team_two, not a repository) but whose input still permits only that second Team is refused the same way - a Team-to-Team promotion cannot silently widen into a Team its material was never permitted to reach, either.",
